<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8' ?>
<!--
  SoftClient4ES :: Tableau Datasource Customization (TDC)

  PURPOSE
  Tell Tableau, up front, that this data source has no temporary tables, so that it goes straight
  to its documented fallback instead of discovering the answer by issuing a CREATE TABLE / DROP
  TABLE probe that SoftClient4ES refuses with an HTTP 400 on every connection.

  WHY SOFTCLIENT4ES HAS NO TEMPORARY TABLES
  An Elasticsearch index is cluster-global, is visible to every client that can read the cluster,
  and has no session scope; ON COMMIT { PRESERVE | DELETE } ROWS is transaction semantics, which
  Elasticsearch does not have. The engine refuses CREATE [LOCAL | GLOBAL] TEMPORARY TABLE by
  intent, naming the construct. See documentation/sql/known_limitations.md.

  THE TRADE-OFF, STATED
  Tableau's fallback for a source without temporary tables uses subqueries, and Tableau's own
  documentation says performance can be poor on large data sets. SoftClient4ES does not accept
  subqueries yet either; relational closure is the next release's work. This file therefore buys a
  clean, immediate "no" instead of a failed probe; it does not make Tableau faster.

  VERIFICATION STATUS, PER CAPABILITY
  read this before you rely on any of it.

    CAP_CREATE_TEMP_TABLES          documented for JDBC connections in Tableau's own JDBC
                                    Capability Customizations Reference.
    CAP_SELECT_INTO                 documented in the same reference.
    CAP_SUPPRESS_TEMP_TABLE_CHECKS  NOT documented for JDBC or ODBC connections. It appears only
                                    in the Tableau Connector SDK capability list, whose
                                    capabilities are declared by a packaged .taco connector, and
                                    SoftClient4ES ships no .taco. Whether a plain TDC on a generic
                                    JDBC connection honours it is UNKNOWN to us. It is included
                                    because it is harmless if ignored, not because it is known to
                                    work.

  NONE OF THIS HAS BEEN EXERCISED AGAINST A LIVE TABLEAU DESKTOP. See the "unverified" subsection
  of documentation/client/bi_tools.md for exactly what would settle it.

  INSTALL
  Copy this file into Tableau's Datasources directory and restart Tableau. The extension must be
  .tdc; the file name itself does not matter.

    Tableau Desktop (Windows)  Documents\My Tableau Repository\Datasources
    Tableau Desktop (macOS)    ~/Documents/My Tableau Repository/Datasources
    Tableau Server (Windows)   ProgramData\Tableau\Tableau Server\data\tabsvc\vizqlserver\Datasources
    Tableau Server (Linux)     /var/opt/tableau/tableau_server/data/tabsvc/vizqlserver/Datasources

  SCOPE
  class and vendor are "genericjdbc", the Other Databases (JDBC) connector. driver is the JDBC
  subprotocol of the connection URL jdbc:elastic://host:port, matching how Tableau's own generic
  JDBC example names the driver. A TDC applies to every connection matching class + vendor +
  driver, so this file affects only Other Databases (JDBC) connections made with the SoftClient4ES
  driver (app.softnetwork.elastic.jdbc.ElasticDriver).
-->
<connection-customization class='genericjdbc' enabled='true' version='10'>
  <vendor name='genericjdbc' />
  <driver name='elastic' />
  <customizations>
    <!-- Tableau must not try to create a temporary table, and must not probe for one at connect. -->
    <customization name='CAP_CREATE_TEMP_TABLES' value='no' />
    <!-- No CREATE TABLE AS from a result set either; same reason. -->
    <customization name='CAP_SELECT_INTO' value='no' />
    <!-- Skip the connection-time capability check outright. UNVERIFIED for a plain TDC: see the
         per-capability note above. -->
    <customization name='CAP_SUPPRESS_TEMP_TABLE_CHECKS' value='yes' />
  </customizations>
</connection-customization>
